ve is $0.$" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510703 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510718 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510703 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510703 1077 "field-1" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510703 1078 #edb/ref 17592186510718 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510703 1079 #uuid "1bc61bdd-576b-5352-ba4d-c3039d7d23da" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510704 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510714 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510704 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510704 1071 "Find $m,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=k(x)$ at the point where $x=0.$\n\nWe have $k(x)=-x^{3} -5 x + 5 e^{x}$ and $k^{\\prime}(x)=-3 x^{2} + 5 e^{x} -5.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510704 1072 #uuid "23f74b85-e755-53c7-b42c-a010cf3710be" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510704 1074 "We have $k(x)=-x^{3} -5 x + 5 e^{x}.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is equal to $k^{\\prime}(0).$ The given derivative is\n\n$$\nk^{\\prime}(x)=-3 x^{2} + 5 e^{x} -5.\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=0$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k^{\\prime}(0) & =-3 (0)^{2} + 5 e^{(0)} -5 \\\\ & =-5+0+5 \\\\ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $0.$" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510705 1080 "2" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510705 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510705 1083 #uuid "3e7afbec-5a92-5243-80c2-e91712f44bfe" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510706 1080 "4" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510706 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510706 1083 #uuid "48da9c19-eb94-57e4-ab53-e522cd3c9230" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510707 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510715 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510707 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510707 1071 "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=2 x^{4} -5 x^{3} -6 x^{2} -\\frac{1}{x}$ at the point where $x=4.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510707 1072 #uuid "5280129d-18fb-5b8f-bb02-d86a2b5535fa" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510707 1074 "Let $f(x)=2 x^{4} -5 x^{3} -6 x^{2} -\\frac{1}{x}.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=4$ is equal to $f^{\\prime}(4).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2 x^{4} -5 x^{3} -6 x^{2} -\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\ & =2\\cdot4x^{3}-5\\cdot3x^{2}-6\\cdot2x+x^{-2} \\\\ & =8 x^{3} -15 x^{2} -12 x + \\frac{1}{x^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=4$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(4) & =8 (4)^{3} -15 (4)^{2} -12 (4) + \\frac{1}{(4)^{2}} \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{16}-240-48+512 \\\\ & =224+\\frac{1}{16} \\\\ & =\\frac{3585}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=4$ is\n\n$$\nm=f^{\\prime}(4)=\\frac{3585}{16}.\n$$" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510708 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510717 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510708 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510708 1071 "Find $m,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=k(x)$ at the point where $x=0.$\n\nWe have $k(x)=-x^{3} -2 x + 6 e^{x}$ and $k^{\\prime}(x)=-3 x^{2} + 6 e^{x} -2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510708 1072 #uuid "689248f2-21f8-5d24-90d8-7ca8fd740f53" 13194139535519 17592186045443 true] [17592186510708 1074 "We have $k(x)=-x^{3} -2 x + 6 e^{x}.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is equal to $k^{\\prime}(0).$ The given derivative is\n\n$$\nk^{\\prime}(x)=-3 x^{2} + 6 e^{x} -2.\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=0$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k^{\\prime}(0) & =-3 (0)^{2} + 6 e^{(0)} -2 \\\\ & =-2+0+6 \\\